Task: Fix Prometheus exporter loopback-only binding (Phase 4)

Summary: PrometheusHttpServer.builder() had no explicit host, defaulting to
127.0.0.1. Confirmed via docker exec + /proc/net/tcp inspection that the
listener was bound to 0100007F (127.0.0.1) not 0.0.0.0 — curl from inside
the same container worked, but Prometheus running in a sibling container
got connection refused. Fixed with .setHost("0.0.0.0"). Verified via
rebuild + docker compose up --force-recreate + Prometheus /api/v1/targets
showing both services "up", then a live query confirming real counts.

Files changed: modules/purerest/src/main/scala/purerest/metrics/Metrics.scala

Why: This is a real correctness bug in already-shipped code from the
original metrics track, invisible until this track's containerization work
actually ran the service across container boundaries instead of on a
single host.
